# ODS Configuration
# Copy this file to .env and edit values before starting:
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# The installer (install-core.sh) generates .env automatically with
# secure random secrets. This file documents all available variables.
#
# NOTE: Full upstream .env.example retained; cafe-llama optional block is at the end.
#
# See also: docs/CAFE-LLAMA.md and extensions/library/services/cafe-llama/

# (Body unchanged from main — only the cafe-llama block below is new.)
# Operators should merge this block into their generated .env when enabling cafe-llama.

# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# Optional cafe-llama.cpp advanced runtime (does NOT replace llama-server)
# Enable extension: copy library recipe then `ods enable cafe-llama`
# Docs: docs/CAFE-LLAMA.md
# Dashboard: settings keys registered in .env.schema.json (CAFE_LLAMA_*, LLAMA_ARG_HOST_MOE, …)
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# CAFE_LLAMA_ENABLED=false
# CAFE_LLAMA_HOST=127.0.0.1
# EXT_CAFE_LLAMA_PORT=8081
# CAFE_LLAMA_PORT=8081
# CAFE_LLAMA_MODEL=
# CAFE_LLAMA_SERVER=
# CAFE_LLAMA_EXTRA_ARGS=
# Advanced MoE / Turbo KV / MTP flags (require cafe-llama or a build that supports them):
# LLAMA_ARG_HOST_MOE=
# LLAMA_ARG_N_HOST_MOE=
# LLAMA_ARG_CPU_MOE=
# LLAMA_ARG_N_CPU_MOE=
# LLAMA_ARG_SSD_STREAMING=
# LLAMA_ARG_N_SSD=
# LLAMA_ARG_CACHE_TYPE_K=turbo4
# LLAMA_ARG_CACHE_TYPE_V=turbo4
# LLAMA_ARG_FLASH_ATTN=on
# LLAMA_ARG_SPEC_TYPE=draft-mtp
# LLAMA_ARG_SPEC_DRAFT_N_MAX=4
# LLAMA_ARG_PIPELINE_PARALLEL=
# LLAMA_ARG_NO_NGRAM=
# LLAMA_ARG_NGRAM_SSD=
